this is one of the most strategic gas  pipelines in the world called Nord  Stream at more than 1,200 kilometers in  length  it connects Russia to Germany and  provides gas to 26 million households in  Europe EU countries import 65% of the  gas consumption mainly from Russia  followed by Norway and Algeria it's a  very strong dependency that forces the  European Union to secure its gas  supplies and avoid any disruptions we  had such a crisis in 2009  previously in 2006 and even some member  states were without gas supply for two  or three weeks and it was a really  dangerous situation for our citizens it  would like to avoid such a situation a  proposal is on the table where in case  of a severe crisis EU states will have  to help their neighbors it's a  solidarity mechanism to protect the most  affected consumers solidarity it means  that in difficult times we can send gas  from one country to another to give  possibility of full gas supply to our  households two most important social  services like hospitals and to some gas  power stations to avoid blackout gas  companies will also be required to be  more transparent the new law will ensure  better cooperation between countries and  a more accurate assessment of common  risks  you
 

